<title>LATVIA: RIGA AIRPORT FIVE MO PASSENGERS UP 5 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>RIGA AIRPORT FIVE MO PASSENGERS UP 5 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Riga airport said on Monday its passenger turnover in the first five months of 1997 rose by five percent to 189,898 compared to the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Viesturs Veinbergs, the commercial manager of the airport, also told Reuters that cargo turnover for the first five months of the year was 237.5 tonnes, roughly the same figure for the corresponding period last year.</p>
<p>National carrier Air Baltic accounted for 20 percent of the airport's passenger flow or 52,000, Veinbergs said.</p>
<p>-- Martinsh Gravitis, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
